{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":3208704,"items":[{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,7,13]],"date-time":"2026-07-13T23:26:15Z","timestamp":1783985175602,"version":"3.55.0"},"reference-count":19,"publisher":"World Scientific Pub Co Pte Lt","issue":"02","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["J. Knot Theory Ramifications"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2010,2]]},"abstract":"<jats:p> We give an alternative presentation of Khovanov homology of links. The original construction rests on the Kauffman bracket model for the Jones polynomial, and the generators for the complex are enhanced Kauffman states. Here we use an oriented sl(2) state model allowing a natural definition of the boundary operator as twisted action of morphisms belonging to a TQFT for trivalent graphs and surfaces. Functoriality in original Khovanov homology holds up to sign. Variants of Khovanov homology fixing functoriality were obtained by Clark\u2013Morrison\u2013Walker [7] and also by Caprau [6]. Our construction is similar to those variants. Here we work over integers, while the previous constructions were over gaussian integers. <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1142\/s0218216510007863","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2010,4,5]],"date-time":"2010-04-05T06:43:13Z","timestamp":1270449793000},"page":"291-312","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":29,"title":["AN ORIENTED MODEL FOR KHOVANOV HOMOLOGY"],"prefix":"10.1142","volume":"19","author":[{"given":"CHRISTIAN","family":"BLANCHET","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Institut de Math\u00e9matiques de Jussieu (UMR-CNRS 7586), Universit\u00e9 Paris Diderot, 175 rue du Chevaleret, F-75013 Paris, France"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"219","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2011,11,21]]},"reference":[{"key":"rf1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.2140\/agt.2002.2.337"},{"key":"rf2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.2140\/gt.2005.9.1443"},{"key":"rf3","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1142\/S0218216507005294"},{"key":"rf4","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.2140\/agt.2006.6.1459"},{"key":"rf5","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/0040-9383(94)00051-4"},{"key":"rf6","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.2140\/agt.2008.8.729"},{"key":"rf7","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.2140\/gt.2009.13.1499"},{"key":"rf8","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.2140\/agt.2004.4.1211"},{"key":"rf9","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1017\/CBO9780511615443"},{"key":"rf10","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1215\/S0012-7094-00-10131-7"},{"key":"rf11","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.2140\/agt.2002.2.665"},{"key":"rf12","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1090\/S0002-9947-05-03665-2"},{"key":"rf13","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.4064\/fm199-1-1"},{"key":"rf14","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.aim.2004.10.015"},{"key":"rf15","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.4213\/im1133"},{"key":"rf16","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1142\/S0218216507005336"},{"key":"rf17","first-page":"325","volume":"44","author":"Murakami H.","journal-title":"Enseign. Math. (2)"},{"key":"rf18","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.2140\/gt.2009.13.1075"},{"key":"rf20","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.4064\/fm184-0-18"}],"container-title":["Journal of Knot Theory and Its Ramifications"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/www.worldscientific.com\/doi\/pdf\/10.1142\/S0218216510007863","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2019,8,6]],"date-time":"2019-08-06T08:15:45Z","timestamp":1565079345000},"score":40.321342,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.worldscientific.com\/doi\/abs\/10.1142\/S0218216510007863"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2010,2]]},"references-count":19,"journal-issue":{"issue":"02","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2011,11,21]]},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2010,2]]}},"alternative-id":["10.1142\/S0218216510007863"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1142\/s0218216510007863","ISSN":["0218-2165","1793-6527"],"issn-type":[{"value":"0218-2165","type":"print"},{"value":"1793-6527","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2010,2]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,29]],"date-time":"2026-09-29T06:27:32Z","timestamp":1790663252246,"version":"4.1.0"},"reference-count":52,"publisher":"Walter de Gruyter GmbH","issue":"787","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2022,6,1]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n               <jats:p>We describe a new geometric model for the Hochschild cohomology of Soergel bimodules based on the monodromic Hecke category studied earlier by the first author and Yun. Moreover, we identify the objects representing individual Hochschild cohomology groups (for the zero and the top degree cohomology this reduces to an earlier result of Gorsky, Hogancamp, Mellit and Nakagane). These objects turn out to be closely related to explicit character sheaves corresponding to exterior powers of the reflection representation of the Weyl group. Applying the described functors to the images of braids in the Hecke category of type A we obtain a geometric description for Khovanov\u2013Rozansky knot homology, essentially different from the one considered earlier by Webster and Williamson.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1515\/crelle-2022-0008","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2022,3,31]],"date-time":"2022-03-31T22:58:31Z","timestamp":1648767511000},"page":"79-124","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":10,"title":["Monodromic model for Khovanov\u2013Rozansky homology"],"prefix":"10.1515","volume":"2022","author":[{"given":"Roman","family":"Bezrukavnikov","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Mathematics , Massachusetts Institute of Technology , 77 Massachusetts Avenue, 02139 , Cambridge , MA , USA"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Kostiantyn","family":"Tolmachov","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Mathematics , University of Edinburgh , James Clerk Maxwell Building, Peter Guthrie Tait Rd, EH9 3FD , Edinburgh , United Kingdom"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"374","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2022,4,1]]},"reference":[{"key":"2023033117480573813_j_crelle-2022-0008_ref_001","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"P.\u2009N.  Achar, A.  Henderson, D.  Juteau and S.  Riche,\nWeyl group actions on the Springer sheaf,\nProc. Lond. Math. Soc. (3) 108 (2014), no. 6, 1501\u20131528.","DOI":"10.1112\/plms\/pdt055"},{"key":"2023033117480573813_j_crelle-2022-0008_ref_002","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"P.\u2009N.  Achar, S.  Riche and C.  Vay,\nMixed perverse sheaves on flag varieties for Coxeter groups,\nCanad. J. Math. 72 (2020), no. 1, 1\u201355.","DOI":"10.4153\/CJM-2018-034-0"},{"key":"2023033117480573813_j_crelle-2022-0008_ref_003","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"S.  Arkhipov and R.  Bezrukavnikov,\nPerverse sheaves on affine flags and Langlands dual group,\nIsrael J. Math. 170 (2009), 135\u2013183.","DOI":"10.1007\/s11856-009-0024-y"},{"key":"2023033117480573813_j_crelle-2022-0008_ref_004","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"A.  Beilinson, R.  Bezrukavnikov and I.  Mirkovi\u0107,\nTilting exercises,\nMosc. Math. J. 4 (2004), no. 3, 547\u2013557.","DOI":"10.17323\/1609-4514-2004-4-3-547-557"},{"key":"2023033117480573813_j_crelle-2022-0008_ref_005","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"A.  Beilinson and V.  Ginzburg,\nWall-crossing functors and \ud835\udc9f\\mathcal{D}-modules,\nRepresent. Theory 3 (1999), 1\u201331.","DOI":"10.1090\/S1088-4165-99-00063-1"},{"key":"2023033117480573813_j_crelle-2022-0008_ref_006","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"A.  